==Personal life==
On March 2, 2007, the Raptors announced that Calderón had been named a Right To Play Athlete Ambassador.<ref name=right>[http://www.nba.com/raptors/community/jose_030207.html "Jose Calderon Named as Right to Play Ambassador"] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070305165847/http://www.nba.com/raptors/community/jose_030207.html |date=March 5, 2007 }}, nba.com/raptors, March 2, 2007, Retrieved June 21, 2007.</ref> Right To Play is an athlete-driven international humanitarian organization that uses sport and play as a tool for the development of children and youth in the most disadvantaged areas of the world.<ref name=right/> As part of the program, Calderón pledged $1000 for every assist he recorded in a home game against the [[Chicago Bulls]] on November 26, 2007. He ended the game with 14 assists.<ref>Smith, Doug, [https://www.thestar.com/Sports/article/279753 "Calderon in a giving mood"], thestar.com, November 26, 2007, Retrieved November 26, 2007.</ref>

Calderon is a co-owner of an organic [[pig farm]].<ref name="hoop">[http://www.nba.com/hoop/24_seconds/24_Seconds_Jose_Calderon-300507-2193.html 24 SECONDS:...with Jose Calderon] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110404210320/http://www.nba.com/hoop/24_seconds/24_Seconds_Jose_Calderon-300507-2193.html |date=April 4, 2011 }}</ref>

He is married to Ana Hurtado. The couple welcomed their first child, Manuel, in [[Villanueva de la Serena]] on May 23, 2010.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://marta-cibelina.blogs.quemedices.diezminutos.es/2010/05/23/jose-manuel-calderon-ya-es-papa/ |title=José Manuel Calderón ya es papá|access-date=April 13, 2011 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110820171250/http://marta-cibelina.blogs.quemedices.diezminutos.es/2010/05/23/jose-manuel-calderon-ya-es-papa/ |archive-date=August 20, 2011 }}</ref>

